{"parentUuid":"c711e5b1-5dfd-4ce2-af76-86ef7448e728","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvQ7wkiKECAXZbKdya1M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The tray works live, but the part where the desktop starts it isn't solved yet.\n\n**What I did for you:**\n- I started a tray by hand, logging to my scratchpad. Its process ID is 64119.\n- I submitted test job j33b65192, which now waits at plan.\n\n**What works:**\n- The white castle is in the menu bar with \"2\" beside it.\n- That count matches the server: j33b65192 waits at plan, and jfbc0b38c has waited at land since the F4 test.\n\n**What I couldn't verify:** the desktop started at 21:02:12 from the new build, so it did run `start_tray`. But no tray was running afterward, and its output went nowhere. In `1719237`, the desktop now sends the tray's output to `tray.log` in Bastion's config folder. A second tray also writes there when it stops because one is already running.\n\n**Please check these yourself, since I can't click the menu or see notifications:**\n1. Did a notification appear for j33b65192 (\"j33b65192 waits for you at plan: …\")?\n2. Does the window title say \"Bastion (2 waiting)\", and does the sidebar show \"Jobs (2)\"?\n3. Open the tray menu. It should read \"2 waiting · … running\", with Approve entries for j33b65192 and jfbc0b38c. Click **Approve j33b65192**. Its plan should be approved and the count should drop.\n4. Click **Pause intake**. The menu should then say \"intake paused\" and offer **Open intake**.\n\n**To test the desktop starting the tray:** run `! cargo build -p bastion-tray -p bastion-desktop`, close the window and start it again. Because the tray I started still holds the lock, the new copy should stop and write \"a Bastion tray already runs\" to `tray.log`. If you'd rather test a clean start, quit my tray first from its menu (\"Quit the tray\"), then restart the desktop.\n\nTell me what you see, and I'll fix anything that's off and record F9 in PLAN.md."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":229,"cache_read_input_tokens":744751,"output_tokens":648,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":229,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":648,"cache_read_input_tokens":744751,"cache_creation_input_tokens":229,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":229},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"76aedaa1-58b2-4fa1-a3f4-78751a78d03e","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgvQ7wQdQjG58hzhgU14Y","type":"assistant","uuid":"815a68ab-40c0-4c0b-b5c4-51d12057272a","timestamp":"2026-11-11T03:04:41.659Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
