{"parentUuid":"a2b9ca24-e19b-4afd-b4d8-a2ee6bded6b7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvQFrVfymr9JM7qWQmA4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KDJjCKfvx4qTpS4G6NsdUD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e/scratchpad; $S/api.sh POST /jobs/$(cat $S/f9job)/stop | tail -1; cd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"| F | F1 to F8 done |\"\nassert a in s; s=s.replace(a,\"| F | F1 to F9 done |\",1)\na=\"and whether a model can look at a screenshot is up to the model and its tools. |\"\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a,\"and whether a model can look at a screenshot is up to the model and its tools. F9 (2026-11-10): a job that comes to wait on a person, fails or lands is a notice: the factory's on_change carries a Change, so beside each job's change it says one line about the job and how many jobs wait. The server publishes notices on its event stream and posts each to a chat webhook as {\\\"text\\\": ...} (Slack, Mattermost), kept in a file only the server's user reads and shown to clients as its host and last four characters; Settings sets it, forgets it and sends a test. bastion-tray is a program of its own on tao and tray-icon, because a tray needs the native event loop iced keeps to itself: it reaches the local server through bastion-client, shows each notice as the system's notification, and its menu says how many jobs wait and run, lists the waiting jobs to approve, pauses or opens intake and opens the window; on macOS the waiting count shows beside a white castle. One runs at a time by a lock, the window starts it with its output in tray.log, and it outlives the window. The window shows the waiting count in its title and on Jobs. The app has an icon: the gh-pages castle with its gate lit (assets/icon). Exit (2026-11-10), live on DeepSeek: a job's plan came to wait, the system notification showed it, the menu bar read the castle and 2, matching the server's two waiting jobs, and the plan was approved and went on to build. The window started the tray once the tray's output was logged; the first start left nothing to say why it stopped. Not run live: the chat webhook (no webhook was set; a test posts a notice to a local listener). The count is in the title and the tray, not a Dock badge, and Open Bastion starts a second window if one is open. |\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit add PLAN.md && git commit -q -m \"F9 is done: notices, a chat webhook, and a tray that watches the factory\" && git log --oneline -1","description":"Stop the test job and record F9"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":639,"cache_read_input_tokens":745809,"output_tokens":1366,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":407},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":639,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1366,"cache_read_input_tokens":745809,"cache_creation_input_tokens":639,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":639},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01KDJjCKfvx4qTpS4G6NsdUD":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e/scratchpad; $S/api.sh POST /jobs/$(cat $S/f9job)/stop | tail -1; cd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"| F | F1 to F8 done |\"\nassert a in s; s=s.replace(a,\"| F | F1 to F9 done |\",1)\na=\"and whether a model can look at a screenshot is up to the model and its tools. 